// MK7 §5: reading a *field* of an owned call temporary. `mkName()` returns a
// `datac` that owns a `String`, and every read below borrows a field of the
// temporary rather than the temporary itself, so nothing else owns it and it
// has to be freed once the statement that read through it is done. The backend
// stages the temporary into a scratch slot so the field has an address, and the
// staging is what leaked: the slot was built and the borrow taken, but no drop
// site was recorded for it, so the `Named` the call returned outlived the
// statement and its `String` was never freed.
//
// The field read here is the `i64` one, which is what makes this fixture a
// *C-buildable* shape: the C backend emits a valid `printf` for a scalar field
// of an rvalue (it does not for an owned field; taking the address of one is
// invalid C, `heap_field_of_owned_temporary.kp`), so the fixture is in the
// valgrind gate. The leak it pins is real in a backend that stages the
// temporary itself, and in the C backend as well: valgrind reports two 3-byte
// losses at `kelp_String__from_str`, one for `print(mkName().r)` and one for
// `take(mkName().r)`, because a `datac` a call returns and the program reads
// only through a field is never dropped. That is BUG-t8Jqr, and this fixture is
// the failing case filed with it rather than a passing one.
datac Named(val r: i64, val name: String)

fun mkName().R: Named = Named(r = 7, name = String.from_str("hi"))

fun take(n: i64) {
    print(n)
}

fun area(n: Named).R: i64 = n.r

fun main() {
    // A field read of a call temporary, in `print` position.
    print(mkName().r)
    // The same temporary read as a call argument.
    take(mkName().r)
    // A field of a temporary passed by borrow as a whole value: the ordinary
    // borrowed-temporary path, which must keep freeing exactly once.
    print(area(mkName()))
    // A field of a *named* local, which is a place and is not a temporary —
    // the borrow stages nothing and nothing may be freed here.
    val n = Named(r = 3, name = String.from_str("bound"))
    print(n.r)
}
